.TH XD\-SCHEDTASKS 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-schedtasks \- Scheduled Tasks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-schedtasks
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-schedtasks
is Windows XP's Scheduled Tasks folder (Control Panel), on systemd user
timers: the user's own service manager, without root.
Add Scheduled Task opens XP's wizard (run a program daily, weekly,
monthly, once, at logon...).
A task's menu runs it, ends it, deletes it or opens its Properties.
Details shows XP's columns: Name, Schedule, Next Run Time, Last Run Time,
Status and Last Result.
.PP
The user's other timers are listed too, read-only.
Tasks that run \(lqWhen I log on\(rq start with
.IR graphical\-session.target .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/systemd/user/xd\-task\-*.timer
.TQ
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/systemd/user/xd\-task\-*.service
A task's timer and service.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd.timer (5),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR xd\-control (1)
